Rationalisation are used to "resolve" traumatic events that otherwise would occasionally add more stress/trauma.
Traumatic events would be diary entries that have recorded high trauma increase
  That would mean depending on traits and insecurities some minor events might end up producing high trauma
  Could have importance treshold for an event to be traumatic, 2 probably but the issue with that is importance customisation is a thing so would mean tracking the default importance or disabling importance customisation until the entry is being written.
  It's mostly the case already but making sure that there isn't more than 1 normal diary entry per event would be more important so that trauma doesn't get split up causing otherwise traumatic event to not count as one.
    Or could just have all events that give even a bit of trauma count and have some method for player to combine them into one entry.

For nice rationalisations there probably needs to be at least some understanding of what the event was ie. Did you successfully resist/escape(and did you even try to)? Did it have an aggressor whose behaviour can be given explanation?
But how far can we get with rationalisations that don't care about what the situation and can be equally applied to any situation.
seeing someone get treated badly, beating up an attacker and having sex
  masturbating in a temple as an angel(+50)
  thinking you are going to get crushed by a trash compactor (+24)
  Being forcibly milked while not cow transformed(+24)
  bracing for it while being branded(+18)
  having your penis size announced(+15 or +10)
  failing to complete a slime task(+12)
  having people thtrow stones at you while you are bound and naked(+12)
  reading a terrible scroll(+12)
  having Kylar break down in tears after you refuse to let him rape you(+12)
  escaping a beast(+12)
  Having police strip you in a street and try to remove your chastity by electrocuting you(+10)
  being seen orgasming in public while embarrased about public nudity(+10)
  Reaching max stress while sleeping(+10)

